@startuml Airports-SD-OwnerCommand
autonumber
title Command forwarded to the owner replica — PATCH /api/airports/{iata}/status (US109; same for US106a, US208)
actor "Backoffice Operator" as BO
participant "airports-1\n: AirportController" as Ctrl
participant ": UpdateAirportService" as Service
participant "airportRepo (H2 #1)" as Repo
participant ": PeerClient" as Peers
participant "airports-2\n(owner of MAD)" as R2
participant "airportRepo (H2 #2)" as Repo2
participant "airports-3" as R3

activate BO
BO -> Ctrl : PATCH /api/airports/MAD/status\n{"status":"UNDER_MAINTENANCE"}
activate Ctrl
Ctrl -> Service : changeStatus("MAD", dto)
activate Service
Service -> Service : AirportStatus.from(dto.status)\n(unknown → 400, before forwarding)
Service -> Repo : findById("MAD")
Repo --> Service : empty (not stored here)

Service -> Peers : forwardToOwner(PATCH, "/api/airports/MAD/status", dto)
activate Peers
note right of Peers
  Unicast: peers are tried ONE AT A TIME.
  Same method, path, body and JWT; X-Peer-Hops: 1.
end note
Peers -> R3 : PATCH /api/airports/MAD/status
R3 -> R3 : hops=1 → no re-forwarding
R3 --> Peers : 404 (not mine) → try next peer
Peers -> R2 : PATCH /api/airports/MAD/status
activate R2
R2 -> Repo2 : findById("MAD")
Repo2 --> R2 : Airport (version 3)
R2 -> R2 : airport.changeStatus(UNDER_MAINTENANCE)
R2 -> Repo2 : saveAndFlush(airport)
note right of Repo2
  @Version: UPDATE ... WHERE version = 3.
  A concurrent change already committed → 409.
end note
Repo2 --> R2 : Airport (version 4)
R2 --> Peers : 200 AirportDTO
deactivate R2
Peers --> Service : Optional(dto)
deactivate Peers
Service --> Ctrl : AirportDTO
deactivate Service
Ctrl --> BO : 200 OK (AirportDTO)
deactivate Ctrl

note over BO, R3
  Single owner: each airport has exactly one copy, so replicas never have conflicting versions.
  Owner answers 4xx (e.g. 409 certification already exists) → same status to the client.
  No replica has the airport → 404. No peer answers → 503.
end note
@enduml
